y that when it was housed within  electrical engineering and computer  science we had a lot of computer science  students come to us and so a lot of the  projects ended up being you know  software related projects because that  was scoffs and that's what they were  comfortable with and but we've also seen  a lot of assistive technology requires  hardware design as well and so that's  why we're bringing in mechanical  engineering support for the class and as  for health sciences and Technology their  role at MIT is really to serve as this  integrative force between different  facets of engineering and the medical  community and so what we're hoping to do  next year with HSTs health science and  technology support is to bring in  occupational therapists into the class  as well to help the students with their  projects so yeah just in thinking about  the different skill sets they go into  the projects we do things software  hardware and then being able to  interface with the health side of things  it's very important
 

